  "description": "The page is configured to use a level\u20112 headline that reads **\u201cExplore <em>{category}</em> articles\u201d** when the site language is set to English, and the current locale is\u202f`en`.  \n\nTwo dynamic selections are defined. The first selection is for **category** (URL parameter\u202f`category`) and draws its list from the resource **news/categories**. Each option is displayed exactly as it appears (`i18nHtmlFormat`\u202f`[0]`, `parameterFormat`\u202f`[0]`) and the underlying data fields are **id** and **name**, supplied by the resource **news/categoryList**. The initial set of categories includes:\n\n- **Technology** (id\u202f`tech`, English name\u202f`Technology`, Spanish name\u202f`Tecnolog\u00eda`)  \n- **Health** (id\u202f`health`, English name\u202f`Health`, Spanish name\u202f`Salud`).\n\nThe second selection concerns **region** (URL parameter\u202f`region`) and uses the resource **news/regions**. Options are rendered inside a `<span>` element (`i18nHtmlFormat`\u202f`<span>{0}</span>`, `parameterFormat`\u202f`{0}`), with the full data payload obtained from **news/regionList** (field path\u202f`/`). No initial region options are pre\u2011loaded."
